            <ArticleTitle>Cerebrospinal fluid leakage after sacral bar removal. A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>91-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A well recognized tool in the management of sacral fractures is the use of extradural sacral bars. This is a case of a previously unreported complication in the use of sacral bars: leakage of cerebrospinal fluid after their removal from a healed fracture.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
